# Shell markup

In `katecms`, `katecms-form`, and `katecms-seo`, layout and text in templates are `div` and `span`. A host site's element CSS must not restyle the CMS shell.

Do not use `p`, headings, `section`, `header`, `footer`, `main`, `nav`, `article`, `aside`, `ul`, `ol`, `li`, `blockquote`, `figure`, or `hr` in our templates. Style with classes, not those selectors.

Leave these as real elements:

- Links: `a`, `NuxtLink`
- Form controls: `form`, `button`, `label`, `input`, `textarea`, `select`, `option`, `optgroup`
- Media: `img`, `picture`, `source`, `svg` and SVG children
- Vue: `template`, `slot`, `component`, `Teleport`

Do not rewrite authored HTML (wysiwyg values, `v-html`) or third-party DOM (Leaflet) into `div`/`span`.
